  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/matthew25187/DataStandardizer",
  "published": "2026-11-23T08:14:05.977Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking changes:\n- `UnM49AreaCodeAttribute.EnglishNames` and `FrenchNames` hold only the area's own name instead of one entry per level, and `Iso3166CountryCodeAttribute.EnglishNames` holds only the English short name instead of the short, upper-case short and full names.\n- Casting a string to Iso3166Part2Subdivision throws InvalidCastException for a code that isn't in ISO 3166-2.\n\nFixed:\n- `GetNativeName` on MM and BY (MMR and BLR) returns the current name instead of the former one (\"Burma\", \"Byelorussian SSR\"), and the ISO 3166-1 enums no longer carry the former names and language rows of Burma, the Byelorussian SSR, Upper Volta, Zaire and East Timor on MM, BY, BF, CD and TL.\n- `UnM49AreaCodeAttribute.EnglishName` and `FrenchName` are the area's own name (such as \"Afghanistan\") instead of \"World\" and \"Monde\", and `Iso3166CountryCodeAttribute.FrenchName` is the country's ISO 3166-1 French short name (such as \"France (la)\") instead of null.\n- Iso3166Part2Enum.GetNames and GetValues return a country's subdivisions sorted by code.\n- Geography name lookups accept a null language code without a nullable warning, as documented.\n- CodeAttributeBase.EnglishNames and FrenchNames return a copy, so changing the returned array no longer changes the attribute's names.\n- The package now includes its XML documentation, so IntelliSense shows member descriptions.",
